  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/AligmentOnManagement"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Determines alignment on who manages, maintains, and oversees data policies/quality"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/AmbiguousDataEntryGuidelines",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual" ],
  "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HasConsequence" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#InconsistentDataEntry;PoorDecisions"
  }, {
    "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/MediumSeverity"
  } ],
  "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HasLikelihood" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HighLikelihood"
  } ],
  "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HasPotentialCause" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/LackOfStandardizedGuidelines"
  } ],
  "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HasSeverity" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/MediumSeverity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/DataEntryAndCollection"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Ambiguities in data entry fields or a lack of standardized guidelines can lead to inconsistent or incorrect data entry. For instance, unclear instructions or inconsistent units of measurement can lead to varying interpretations and inaccurate data entries. The consequences, as discussed in the literature, include data inconsistencies that can mislead clinicians and affect the accuracy of diagnoses and treatments.\n\n The severity of ambiguous data entry guidelines escalates from medium to high, as reflected in the ECG management consultants’ report, through the complications arising from non-standardized data entries that could lead to varied interpretations and, hence, inconsistent healthcare delivery. However, ambiguous guidelines usually have a medium impact because they can lead to inconsistent data entries, which may compromise data quality but not always directly affect patient safety. The likelihood of ambiguous guidelines is often high due to varying interpretations by different users or departments within healthcare settings, with medium detectability, as discrepancies can usually be identified through audits or when data fails to meet expected standards during quality checks. The Pharma Daily report mentioned in their regulatory guidelines and standards that a lack of clarity in definitions and guidelines can lead to variations in data entry, thus impacting clinical data management. This report highlighted the need for clear data management guidelines to prevent ambiguous entries, as discussed in the context of clinical data management standards and the importance of regulatory adherence."
  } ]
}, {
